{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519516-the-nameless-empire-and-the-5-9-ky-event","id":519516,"title":"The Nameless Empire and the 5.9 ky Event","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-19T06:55:41-07:00","id":519516,"title":"The Nameless Empire and the 5.9 ky Event","content":"Alright, so I've been working on a timeline of both real world history and the history of the World of Darkness, both out of interest, and because it results in some neat plot ideas for when I'm storytelling. I think I've found yet another one.<br /> <br /> Here are some baseless assumptions I've made before I start detailing it:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The Nameless Empire lasted less than a full Sothic Turn and while it was a long lived Empire, due to supernatural aid and being fairly well run, it was still comparable to some real long lasting empires and nations.</li> <li>The Rite of Return began about a century before it was completed, but the final true ritual occurred in 3832 BCE, when Irem vanished, on the Sothic Turn.</li> <li>Azer's murder occurred exactly one Sothic turn before Irem's fall.</li> </ol>Using these, and some of my own creative license, I've come up with this section of Mummy dates which are in gold (it seemed appropriate):<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://orig15.deviantart.net/9dc2/f/2015/139/c/a/nameless_empire_and_5_9_ky_event_by_peace__out-d8tybvq.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Purple are nations/civilizations/culture groups. Blue are historical events and time periods. What's most interesting to me right now, and what I discovered today through some research, is on the bottom in brown, which is code for geological events.<br /> <br /> This all comes out of being introduced to the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahara_pump_theory\" target=\"_blank\">Sahara Pump Hypothesis</a>, which helps to explain human migration out of Africa based on climate change. Basically, the Sahara hasn't always been desert and it goes through cycles. When it is in its wet phase, its more like a savannah, and humans migrate into it, but when it switches back to a desert, they all hightail it for better places to live (unless you are on the Nile). The last time it switched over was during what is known as the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5.9_kiloyear_event\" target=\"_blank\">5.9 KY Event</a>. This event created the Sahara as we know it today, a dry desert that is very tough to live in. Since we don't actually know when it was, I've put error bars of about plus/minus one hundred years on my timeline, although I may trim that down.<br /> <br /> Point is, this matches the timeline of Irem's fall pretty closely. A later event, the 4.2 KY Event, also on the graph, is widely believed to have lead to the fall of Old Kingdom Egypt (protip: century long droughts in the desert are not fun). Could it be 5.9 KY changed the lives of our Mummies? Could the Rite of Return been responsible for the event itself? What would Irem have been like if the Sahara were more habitable? I know these questions aren't for everyone and that's okay. Use as much or as little historical accuracy in your games as you like. I'm intrigued by these possibilities though and would love to hear other's thoughts on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 05-19-2015, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T07:38:19-07:00","id":519553,"title":"","content":"I don't know if your image is showing properly, is just a small box saying Adult Role Playing elliquiy.com.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T13:25:38-07:00","id":519954,"title":"","content":"I actually agree on this theory whole heartedly. I mean, Irem is said to have been &quot;swallowed by the sands&quot;. While the main capital was probably just.. shifted straight into Duat, the bulk of the empire going from savannah to desert would probably mess up any survivors, most cities, etc. I'lleven go a step further and say Irem and the Rite was responsible for a flooding as well, known throughout the fertile crescent and Levant. The Rite supposedly broke time itself, so side effects like the Sahara's desertification and the Deluge aren't that unfeasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T01:15:21-07:00","id":525262,"title":"","content":"I'm onboard. Also in terms of history - this came up in discussion of Proto-Scythians on another thread, and doing some digging I realized that the proto-scythians on the north side of the Black Sea would be the proto-Indo-Aryans in general at this point. My new ruling at my own table is that the power vacuum created by the fall of the Nameless Empire (and the 5.9 ky event) is what triggered their expansion, eventually bringing them down on the heads of the Indus River Valley civilization (which I may make another collapsed Awakened attempt at their lost utopia).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title